`,e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["This article looks at a fundamental challenge in modern trading systems: ",e.jsx(s.strong,{children:"markets change quickly, while the systems analysing them have a finite amount of time and computing capacity to decide what is still worth acting on"}),". The examples use Rust and decentralized finance (DeFi), but the principles apply much more broadly to trading platforms and distributed systems built in any language."]}),`
